       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is 5 times the maximum labeled dose. I know of no indication that justifies it, and it could seriously harm the patient. You also haven't given a clinical rationale, such as a toxicology recommendation or a protocol.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can enter 50, 100, or 200 mg PO daily right away.\n- **Get a second opinion.** If you think there's a reason for a supratherapeutic dose, please discuss it with the attending, psychiatry, or clinical pharmacy first. I can enter the order once they've agreed on a dose.\n- **Enter it yourself.** If you still want to order it as written, you can do so directly in the order-entry system. It will go through the pharmacy verification process, and I'd expect pharmacy to flag it.\n\nIf the patient may have taken an overdose, please contact poison control or toxicology. I can help with orders for monitoring or supportive care."
